# source = Plato, Crito_44
# text = ὡς ἐμοί , ἐὰν σὺ ἀποθάνῃς , οὐ μία συμφορά ἐστιν , ἀλλὰ χωρὶς μὲν τοῦ ἐστερῆσθαι τοιούτου ἐπιτηδείου οἷον ἐγὼ οὐδένα μή ποτε εὑρήσω , ἔτι δὲ καὶ πολλοῖς δόξω , οἳ ἐμὲ καὶ σὲ μὴ σαφῶς ἴσασιν , ὡς οἷός τʼ ὤν σε σῴζειν εἰ ἤθελον ἀναλίσκειν χρήματα , ἀμελῆσαι [0] .
# sent_id = 65
# subdoc = 44c.1
# literal_translation = As for me, if you die, not one misfortune is it, but apart from being deprived of such a companion as I shall never find again, and besides to many I shall seem, who do not know me and you clearly, that though I was able to save you if I had been willing to spend money, I neglected [it].
# readable_translation = For me, if you die, it is not just one misfortune, but apart from being deprived of such a companion as I shall never find again, and besides, many people who do not know me and you well will think that, though I was able to save you if I had been willing to spend money, I neglected to do so.
