# source = Plato, Crito_45
# text = ὡς ἔγωγε καὶ ὑπὲρ σοῦ καὶ ὑπὲρ ἡμῶν τῶν σῶν ἐπιτηδείων αἰσχύνομαι μὴ δόξῃ ἅπαν τὸ πρᾶγμα τὸ περὶ σὲ ἀνανδρίᾳ τινὶ τῇ ἡμετέρᾳ πεπρᾶχθαι , καὶ ἡ εἴσοδος τῆς δίκης εἰς τὸ δικαστήριον ὡς εἰσῆλθεν ἐξὸν μὴ εἰσελθεῖν , καὶ αὐτὸς ὁ ἀγὼν τῆς δίκης ὡς ἐγένετο , καὶ τὸ τελευταῖον δὴ τουτί , ὥσπερ κατάγελως τῆς πράξεως , κακίᾳ τινὶ καὶ ἀνανδρίᾳ τῇ ἡμετέρᾳ διαπεφευγέναι ἡμᾶς δοκεῖν , οἵτινές σε οὐχὶ ἐσώσαμεν οὐ δὲ σὺ σαυτόν , οἷόν τε ὂν καὶ δυνατὸν εἴ τι καὶ μικρὸν ἡμῶν ὄφελος ἦν [0] [1] [2] .
# sent_id = 102
# subdoc = 45e.1
# literal_translation = For I at least am ashamed both on your behalf and on behalf of us, your companions, lest it should seem that the whole affair concerning you has been done by some cowardice of ours, and the entrance of the case into the court, how it came in when it was possible not to come in, and the contest of the case itself, how it happened, and this last thing, as a mockery of the action, that by some baseness and cowardice of ours it has escaped us, so that we seem not to have saved you, nor you yourself, when it was possible and feasible if there was even some small help from us [would have been] [saved] [you].
# readable_translation = For I am ashamed, both on your behalf and on behalf of us, your friends, that the whole affair concerning you might seem to have been carried out with a certain cowardice on our part: the way the case came into court when it could have been kept out, the way the trial itself was conducted, and finally this last thing, as a mockery of the whole business, that through some baseness and cowardice of ours it seems to have slipped away from us, since we did not save you, nor did you save yourself, when it was possible and feasible, if there was even a little help from us.
