# source = Plato, Crito_48
# text = ἡμῖν δʼ , ἐπειδὴ ὁ λόγος οὕτως αἱρεῖ , μὴ οὐδὲν ἄλλο σκεπτέον ᾖ ἢ ὅπερ νυνδὴ ἐλέγομεν , πότερον δίκαια πράξομεν καὶ χρήματα τελοῦντες τούτοις τοῖς ἐμὲ ἐνθένδε ἐξάξουσιν καὶ χάριτας , καὶ αὐτοὶ ἐξάγοντές τε καὶ ἐξαγόμενοι , ἢ τῇ ἀληθείᾳ ἀδικήσομεν πάντα ταῦτα ποιοῦντες [0] ·
# sent_id = 207
# subdoc = 48d.1
# literal_translation = But for us, since the argument thus chooses, nothing else must be examined than just what we were saying just now: whether we will do just things, both paying money and thanks to those who will lead me out from here, and ourselves both leading out and being led out, or in truth we will do wrong doing all these things;
# readable_translation = But for us, since the argument thus decides, we must examine nothing else than what we were just saying: whether we will act justly in paying money and gratitude to those who will lead me out of here, and in ourselves both leading and being led out, or whether in truth we will be doing wrong in doing all these things;
