# source = Plato, Crito_49
# text = σκόπει δὴ οὖν καὶ σὺ εὖ μάλα πότερον κοινωνεῖς καὶ συνδοκεῖ σοι καὶ ἀρχώμεθα ἐντεῦθεν βουλευόμενοι , ὡς οὐδέποτε ὀρθῶς ἔχοντος οὔ τε τοῦ ἀδικεῖν οὔ τε τοῦ ἀνταδικεῖν οὔ τε κακῶς πάσχοντα ἀμύνεσθαι ἀντιδρῶντα κακῶς , ἢ ἀφίστασαι καὶ οὐ κοινωνεῖς τῆς ἀρχῆς ;
# sent_id = 254
# subdoc = 49d.4
# literal_translation = Consider then also you very well whether you share and it seems good to you and we should begin from there deliberating, as never rightly having either the doing-wrong or the doing-wrong-in-return or when suffering badly to defend oneself by doing badly in return, or you stand off and do not share the principle;
# readable_translation = Consider then, and you too, very carefully whether you share this view and it seems good to you, and we should begin our deliberation from there, that it is never right either to do wrong or to return wrong for wrong or, when one is treated badly, to defend oneself by doing bad in return; or do you stand apart and not share this principle?
