# source = Plato, Crito_51
# text = ἢ πρὸς μὲν ἄρα σοι τὸν πατέρα οὐκ ἐξ ἴσου ἦν τὸ δίκαιον καὶ πρὸς δεσπότην , εἴ σοι ὢν ἐτύγχανεν , ὥστε ἅπερ πάσχοις ταῦτα καὶ ἀντιποιεῖν , οὔ τε κακῶς ἀκούοντα ἀντιλέγειν οὔ τε τυπτόμενον ἀντιτύπτειν οὔ τε ἄλλα τοιαῦτα πολλά [0] ·
# sent_id = 299
# subdoc = 51a.1
# literal_translation = Or toward on the one hand then to you the father not from equal was the just and toward master, if to you being he happened, so that whatever you might suffer these things also to do in return, neither being spoken ill of to speak against nor being struck to strike back nor other such many [was it]?
# readable_translation = Or then, was the just not on equal terms for you toward your father and toward a master, if you happened to have one, so that whatever you suffered you could do in return, neither answering back when spoken ill of nor striking back when struck nor doing many other such things?
