# source = Plato, Crito_51
# text = πρὸς δὲ τὴν πατρίδα ἄρα καὶ τοὺς νόμους ἐξέσται σοι , ὥστε , ἐάν σε ἐπιχειρῶμεν ἡμεῖς ἀπολλύναι δίκαιον ἡγούμενοι εἶναι , καὶ σὺ δὲ ἡμᾶς τοὺς νόμους καὶ τὴν πατρίδα καθʼ ὅσον δύνασαι ἐπιχειρήσεις ἀνταπολλύναι , καὶ φήσεις ταῦτα ποιῶν δίκαια πράττειν , ὁ τῇ ἀληθείᾳ τῆς ἀρετῆς ἐπιμελόμενος ;
# sent_id = 300
# subdoc = 51a.2
# literal_translation = Against the fatherland then and the laws will it be permitted to you, so that, if we undertake to destroy you, considering it just to be, you too will undertake to destroy us the laws and the fatherland as far as you can, and will say that in doing these things you do just things, you who in truth cares for virtue?
# readable_translation = Then will it be permitted to you against your fatherland and the laws, so that, if we undertake to destroy you, thinking it just, you too will undertake to destroy us, the laws and your fatherland, as far as you can, and will say that in doing these things you are acting justly—you who truly cares for virtue?
