# source = Plato, Crito_52
# text = ἄλλο τι οὖν , ἂν φαῖεν , ἢ συνθήκας τὰς πρὸς ἡμᾶς αὐτοὺς καὶ ὁμολογίας παραβαίνεις , οὐχ ὑπὸ ἀνάγκης ὁμολογήσας οὐ δὲ ἀπατηθεὶς οὐ δὲ ἐν ὀλίγῳ χρόνῳ ἀναγκασθεὶς βουλεύσασθαι , ἀλλʼ ἐν ἔτεσιν ἑβδομήκοντα , ἐν οἷς ἐξῆν σοι ἀπιέναι , εἰ μὴ ἠρέσκομεν ἡμεῖς μη δὲ δίκαιαι ἐφαίνοντό σοι αἱ ὁμολογίαι εἶναι .
# sent_id = 329
# subdoc = 52e.1
# literal_translation = Anything other then, they-would-say, than the-agreements the with-us themselves and agreements you-transgress, not under necessity having-agreed nor having-been-deceived nor in little time having-been-forced to-deliberate, but in years seventy, in which it-was-possible for-you to-go-away, if not we-were-pleasing we nor just they-were-appearing to-you the agreements to-be.
# readable_translation = Then, they would say, are you not breaking the compacts and agreements you made with us, though you were not forced to agree, nor deceived, nor compelled to decide in a short time, but had seventy years, during which you could have gone away if we did not please you and if the agreements did not seem just to you?
